287
00:09:29,564 --> 00:09:32,201
This stops new emergencies from becoming new

288
00:09:32,201 --> 00:09:32,501
debt.

289
00:09:32,681 --> 00:09:34,479
Automate a transfer on payday,

290
00:09:34,479 --> 00:09:35,618
even if it's small.

291
00:09:35,968 --> 00:09:37,265
If it feels slow,

292
00:09:37,265 --> 00:09:39,325
speed it up with a one time

293
00:09:39,325 --> 00:09:39,707
push.

294
00:09:39,887 --> 00:09:41,635
Sell things you don't use,

295
00:09:41,635 --> 00:09:42,981
take an extra shift,

296
00:09:42,981 --> 00:09:45,200
or put a tax refund straight into

297
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:45,402
it.

298
00:09:45,582 --> 00:09:48,055
Most people can finish this step within

299
00:09:48,055 --> 00:09:48,879
a few months.

300
00:09:49,228 --> 00:09:50,157
Step three.

301
00:09:50,337 --> 00:09:52,067
Get the full employer match.

302
00:09:52,417 --> 00:09:54,813
If your employer offers a retirement plan

303
00:09:54,813 --> 00:09:57,151
match, contribute at least enough to get

304
00:09:57,151 --> 00:09:57,735
all of it.

305
00:09:57,915 --> 00:10:00,248
A match is part of your compensation.

306
00:10:00,428 --> 00:10:02,365
Not taking it is like turning down

307
00:10:02,365 --> 00:10:02,820
a raise.

308
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,087
On a sixty thousand dollar salary,

309
00:10:05,087 --> 00:10:07,296
a four percent match is two thousand

310
00:10:07,296 --> 00:10:09,014
four hundred dollars a year.

311
00:10:09,364 --> 00:10:11,834
Check your plan's vesting schedule too,

312
00:10:11,834 --> 00:10:13,923
which tells you how long you need

313
00:10:13,923 --> 00:10:16,772
to stay to keep the employer's contributions.

314
00:10:16,952 --> 00:10:19,642
And if your employer doesn't offer a

315
00:10:19,642 --> 00:10:21,810
plan, an IRA is the next best

316
00:10:21,810 --> 00:10:22,931
place to start.

317
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:24,174
Step four.

318
00:10:24,354 --> 00:10:25,841
Kill high interest debt.

319
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:28,998
List every debt above roughly eight percent

320
00:10:28,998 --> 00:10:31,218
interest, especially credit cards.

321
00:10:31,398 --> 00:10:33,171
Pay minimums on all of them,

322
00:10:33,171 --> 00:10:35,325
and send every extra dollar to the

323
00:10:35,325 --> 00:10:36,529
highest rate first.

324
00:10:36,709 --> 00:10:38,716
Paying off a card at twenty two

325
00:10:38,716 --> 00:10:41,434
percent is a guaranteed twenty two percent

326
00:10:41,434 --> 00:10:41,887
return.

327
00:10:42,237 --> 00:10:43,544
When one is paid off,

328
00:10:43,544 --> 00:10:45,535
roll that payment into the next.

329
00:10:45,715 --> 00:10:48,491
You're already used to living without that

330
00:10:48,491 --> 00:10:50,475
money, so the momentum builds.

331
00:10:50,655 --> 00:10:53,143
Many people clear thousands of dollars of

332
00:10:53,143 --> 00:10:54,963
debt within a year or two this

333
00:10:54,963 --> 00:10:55,206
way.

334
00:10:55,555 --> 00:10:56,554
Step five.

335
00:10:56,734 --> 00:10:58,661
Right size the big three.

336
00:10:59,011 --> 00:11:00,210
Look at housing,

337
00:11:00,210 --> 00:11:02,007
transportation and food.

338
00:11:02,187 --> 00:11:05,062
Many planners suggest keeping housing around a

339
00:11:05,062 --> 00:11:07,125
quarter to under a third of gross

340
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:07,562
income.

341
00:11:07,742 --> 00:11:09,204
On sixty thousand dollars,

342
00:11:09,204 --> 00:11:11,791
that's roughly twelve hundred fifty to sixteen

343
00:11:11,791 --> 00:11:13,141
hundred dollars a month.

344
00:11:13,321 --> 00:11:15,895
Cars, including insurance and gas,

345
00:11:15,895 --> 00:11:18,545
ideally well under fifteen percent.

346
00:11:18,895 --> 00:11:20,876
You don't have to fix everything at

347
00:11:20,876 --> 00:11:21,159
once.

348
00:11:21,339 --> 00:11:23,047
At your next lease renewal,

349
00:11:23,047 --> 00:11:25,449
consider a cheaper unit or a roommate.

350
00:11:25,629 --> 00:11:27,146
When your car loan ends,

351
00:11:27,146 --> 00:11:28,474
keep driving the car.

352
00:11:28,654 --> 00:11:30,964
Cook a few more meals at home.

353
00:11:31,144 --> 00:11:33,187
One big change in the big three

354
00:11:33,187 --> 00:11:35,098
can be worth more than a year

355
00:11:35,098 --> 00:11:36,020
of small cuts.

356
00:11:36,370 --> 00:11:37,497
Step six.

357
00:11:37,677 --> 00:11:39,685
Build the full emergency fund.

358
00:11:40,035 --> 00:11:42,093
Grow your cushion to three to six

359
00:11:42,093 --> 00:11:43,902
months of essential expenses.

360
00:11:44,082 --> 00:11:46,454
On an average salary with essential costs

361
00:11:46,454 --> 00:11:48,768
of about three thousand dollars a month,

362
00:11:48,768 --> 00:11:51,140
that's nine to eighteen thousand dollars.

363
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,261
More if your income is irregular or

364
00:11:53,261 --> 00:11:54,536
you're the only earner.

365
00:11:54,886 --> 00:11:57,093
This is what lets you keep investing

366
00:11:57,093 --> 00:11:58,319
through job changes,

367
00:11:58,319 --> 00:12:01,139
car repairs and medical bills without touching

368
00:12:01,139 --> 00:12:03,652
your investments or going back into debt.

369
00:12:03,832 --> 00:12:06,340
It's the wall that protects everything else.

370
00:12:06,689 --> 00:12:07,734
Step seven.

371
00:12:07,914 --> 00:12:10,324
Invest fifteen percent of your income,

372
00:12:10,324 --> 00:12:11,212
automatically.

373
00:12:11,561 --> 00:12:15,335
Raise your retirement contributions toward fifteen percent

374
00:12:15,335 --> 00:12:16,181
of gross pay,

375
00:12:16,181 --> 00:12:17,483
including the match.

376
00:12:17,663 --> 00:12:19,550
Use your workplace plan,

377
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:20,809
an IRA, or both.

378
00:12:20,989 --> 00:12:23,298
Choose simple, diversified,

379
00:12:23,298 --> 00:12:24,580
low cost funds,

380
00:12:24,580 --> 00:12:27,744
like broad index funds or target date

381
00:12:27,744 --> 00:12:28,257
funds.

382
00:12:28,606 --> 00:12:31,217
If fifteen percent isn't possible yet,

383
00:12:31,217 --> 00:12:33,347
start where you can and add one

384
00:12:33,347 --> 00:12:35,065
percent every six months,

385
00:12:35,065 --> 00:12:37,676
or turn on automatic increases if your

386
00:12:37,676 --> 00:12:38,638
plan has them.

387
00:12:38,818 --> 00:12:40,601
You'll barely notice each step,

388
00:12:40,601 --> 00:12:41,694
but in a few years,

389
00:12:41,694 --> 00:12:42,614
you'll be there.

390
00:12:42,963 --> 00:12:43,718
Step eight.

391
00:12:43,898 --> 00:12:45,593
Use tax advantages.

392
00:12:45,943 --> 00:12:48,401
Tax advantaged accounts can make a big

393
00:12:48,401 --> 00:12:50,471
difference on an average salary.

394
00:12:50,651 --> 00:12:54,268
A 401k or traditional IRA can lower

395
00:12:54,268 --> 00:12:55,818
your taxes now.

396
00:12:55,998 --> 00:12:58,605
A Roth IRA or Roth 401k can

397
00:12:58,605 --> 00:13:01,791
make future withdrawals tax free,

398
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:03,335
under IRS rules.

399
00:13:03,515 --> 00:13:06,040
Many people on moderate incomes find a

400
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:07,833
Roth especially attractive,

401
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:10,158
because their tax rate today may be

402
00:13:10,158 --> 00:13:11,155
relatively low.

403
00:13:11,504 --> 00:13:13,738
If you have a high deductible health

404
00:13:13,738 --> 00:13:16,220
plan, a health savings account can offer

405
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,275
tax benefits too.

406
00:13:17,455 --> 00:13:20,039
And low and moderate income savers may

407
00:13:20,039 --> 00:13:22,147
qualify for the Saver's Credit,

408
00:13:22,147 --> 00:13:25,547
a federal tax credit for retirement contributions.

409
00:13:25,727 --> 00:13:28,353
Check the IRS website for current rules

410
00:13:28,353 --> 00:13:29,094
and limits.

411
00:13:29,443 --> 00:13:30,442
Step nine.

412
00:13:30,622 --> 00:13:31,818
Grow your income.

413
00:13:32,167 --> 00:13:33,558
On an average salary,

414
00:13:33,558 --> 00:13:36,205
income growth is often the most powerful

415
00:13:36,205 --> 00:13:36,602
lever.

416
00:13:36,782 --> 00:13:39,167
Ask for raises with evidence of your

417
00:13:39,167 --> 00:13:39,697
results.

418
00:13:39,877 --> 00:13:42,233
Learn skills your industry pays more for.

419
00:13:42,413 --> 00:13:43,760
Get a certification.

420
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:45,757
Consider changing employers,

421
00:13:45,757 --> 00:13:48,223
which often brings a larger raise than

422
00:13:48,223 --> 00:13:49,002
staying put.

423
00:13:49,352 --> 00:13:50,908
And apply a raise rule.

424
00:13:51,088 --> 00:13:53,195
Send at least half of every raise

425
00:13:53,195 --> 00:13:54,792
to savings and investing.

426
00:13:54,972 --> 00:13:56,947
Your lifestyle still improves,

427
00:13:56,947 --> 00:13:59,581
but your savings rate climbs every year.

428
00:13:59,761 --> 00:14:02,578
That's how average salaries become above average

429
00:14:02,578 --> 00:14:02,989
wealth.

430
00:14:03,338 --> 00:14:04,198
Step ten.

431
00:14:04,378 --> 00:14:05,817
Protect what you build.

432
00:14:06,167 --> 00:14:07,688
Have health insurance.

433
00:14:07,868 --> 00:14:09,917
If people depend on your income,

434
00:14:09,917 --> 00:14:12,478
consider affordable term life insurance.

435
00:14:12,658 --> 00:14:14,565
Consider disability insurance,

436
00:14:14,565 --> 00:14:16,917
which replaces part of your income if

437
00:14:16,917 --> 00:14:17,870
you can't work.

438
00:14:18,050 --> 00:14:20,268
Many employers offer it cheaply.

439
00:14:20,617 --> 00:14:23,087
Name beneficiaries on every account and keep

440
00:14:23,087 --> 00:14:23,984
them up to date.

441
00:14:24,164 --> 00:14:25,906
And consider a basic will.

442
00:14:26,086 --> 00:14:27,600
These steps cost little,

443
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,672
take a few hours,

444
00:14:28,672 --> 00:14:30,312
and protect years of work.

445
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:31,521
Step eleven.

446
00:14:31,701 --> 00:14:33,593
Avoid the big mistakes.

447
00:14:33,942 --> 00:14:36,298
The biggest threats to wealth on an

448
00:14:36,298 --> 00:14:38,654
average salary are a handful of big

449
00:14:38,654 --> 00:14:39,260
mistakes.

450
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:43,085
Cashing out retirement accounts when changing jobs.

451
00:14:43,265 --> 00:14:45,459
Buying a house or car far above

452
00:14:45,459 --> 00:14:46,238
your means.

453
00:14:46,418 --> 00:14:48,497
Co signing loans you can't afford to

454
00:14:48,497 --> 00:14:48,844
cover.

455
00:14:49,024 --> 00:14:51,402
Putting a large share of savings into

456
00:14:51,402 --> 00:14:52,623
a single risky bet.

457
00:14:52,973 --> 00:14:55,702
And panic selling during a market crash.

458
00:14:55,882 --> 00:14:57,208
Write your plan now:

459
00:14:57,208 --> 00:14:58,667
when the market falls,

460
00:14:58,667 --> 00:14:59,794
I keep investing.

461
00:14:59,974 --> 00:15:01,054
Then follow it.

462
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:03,721
Avoiding a few big mistakes matters more

463
00:15:03,721 --> 00:15:05,959
than finding the perfect investment.

464
00:15:06,309 --> 00:15:07,273
Step twelve.

465
00:15:07,453 --> 00:15:09,206
Stay the course for decades.

466
00:15:09,556 --> 00:15:11,794
This is the step that turns everything

467
00:15:11,794 --> 00:15:12,796
else into wealth.

468
00:15:12,976 --> 00:15:16,581
Keep the automatic contributions running for twenty,

469
00:15:16,581 --> 00:15:17,968
thirty, forty years.

470
00:15:18,148 --> 00:15:19,286
Review once a quarter.

471
00:15:19,466 --> 00:15:21,149
Adjust when life changes.

472
00:15:21,329 --> 00:15:22,235
But don't stop.

473
00:15:22,584 --> 00:15:24,291
Remember the shape of the curve.

474
00:15:24,471 --> 00:15:25,645
Slow for years,

475
00:15:25,645 --> 00:15:27,211
then suddenly steep.

476
00:15:27,391 --> 00:15:28,743
On an average salary,

477
00:15:28,743 --> 00:15:31,189
the steep part usually arrives in your

478
00:15:31,189 --> 00:15:32,476
