915
00:29:53,708 --> 00:29:54,800
They let you keep going.

916
00:29:55,149 --> 00:29:56,392
Objection three.

917
00:29:56,572 --> 00:29:58,808
A million dollars won't be worth much

918
00:29:58,808 --> 00:30:00,078
in thirty five years.

919
00:30:00,258 --> 00:30:03,277
It's true that inflation reduces purchasing power.

920
00:30:03,457 --> 00:30:05,001
At three percent inflation,

921
00:30:05,001 --> 00:30:07,174
a million dollars in thirty five years

922
00:30:07,174 --> 00:30:09,576
might buy what roughly three hundred fifty

923
00:30:09,576 --> 00:30:11,177
thousand dollars buys today.

924
00:30:11,357 --> 00:30:13,772
But that's exactly why investing matters.

925
00:30:13,952 --> 00:30:16,170
Cash in a drawer loses value.

926
00:30:16,350 --> 00:30:18,968
Investments have historically been one of the

927
00:30:18,968 --> 00:30:21,063
